0.10.0 — the renderer IS the model: positions are written by JS (rAF + 4fps planner-tick fallback for background tabs) straight from the reservation arithmetic, one clock, no CSS motion engine to drift. Mirror/pinwheel moved to an inner wrapper — scale/rotate must never share a transform with a translation (they multiply it and teleport the glyph). Safari-safe
0.10.1 — the mirror/spin wrapper is a <u>, which underlines by default; text-decoration: none on .cr-g u
0.11.0 — stubborn streams: a dealt share (opt.stubbornP, default 0.35) are commissioned to exit by the edge opposite their entry. They still yield to traffic, but a wrong edge is a wall, and they steer back toward the target at the next clear square. Past their wander budget they give up and leave by any edge — the release valve against gridlock
0.12.0 — the lab bench: stubborn-share slider (live — changes what the planner deals next, no remount), streams dial up to 64, and pause/play/reset. Pause freezes the piece's own clock, so resume continues from the exact frozen instant
0.12.1 — streams dial max raised to 256; saturation shows around ~190 concurrent on a desktop sheet, the placed readout tells the story
0.13.0 — the mini: mini.php, the same engine iframed at junk-drawer loading-card size (the darkroom swatch, ~41% x 33% of a card). Zoom 1 — the house 9px grid, so the paper and every script shrink together; the sheet fills its frame and re-deals on resize. n/stubborn query params for tuning
0.13.1 — the mini grows up: opened directly it caps at swatch size (300x243) on white with the lab bench beneath (streams / stubborn / pause / reset, same dials as the piece page); iframed it still fills its frame edge to edge and shows no chrome. Solo is detected with window === window.top, the CSS keys off html.is-solo
0.14.0 — word mode (opt.words): every stream IS a word from the list — its length is the spelling, letters dealt once at birth, head letter first so it reads in arrival order around every turn; a space travels as a blank square. No mirrors, no pinwheels, no re-strikes (a changed letter is a misprint). Speeds now per-mount via opt.speedMin/speedSpan. mockup-34-word-mesh.html exercises it
0.14.1 — word reading order is SPATIAL, not arrival (owner, 2026-08-23): horizontals read left-to-right, verticals top-to-bottom, whichever way the string travels — so the leading letter is the word's last for east/south-bound streams, its first for west/north-bound
0.14.2 — no more U-turns: a turn may never reverse the entry axis (two perpendiculars used to fold a path back on itself, and a folded word reads against its own letters). Applies in both modes; sims still clean at 8 and 32, axis balance holds
0.14.3 — the TEMP red ink retires: stubborn streams wear the same blue as everyone (tuning settled; the is-stubborn class and its rule are gone). mockup-34 defaults: 14 streams, 2.8-5 cells/sec, 100% stubborn, zoom 2, the sixteen wait-words
0.14.4 — word streams all wear the same ink: the per-stream opacity lottery (0.62-1.0, the character rain's depth cue) is pinned to 1 in word mode (owner, 2026-08-23)
0.14.5 — word mode: no word twice on one sheet (owner call, via the darkroom). The planner deals a birth only from the words not currently live — a string re-enters only after its instance has left — and when every word is out the slot waits its turn, the same discipline as clear spacetime
